blocks.body:
**Why is *elohim* plural?** Explanations include:

- a *plural of majesty* or fullness, expressing God's greatness (common grammatical view);
- an echo of the divine council, the heavenly host over which God presides;
- a hint of plurality within God, read by many Church Fathers in the light of "Let us make man in our image" (Gen 1:26) and later Trinitarian faith.

Most scholars think the grammar alone does not prove the Trinity, though Christians have long read it as open to it.
